# Build context for `docker build -f scraper/Dockerfile .` is the repo root,
# so Docker reads THIS file (NOT scraper/.dockerignore — Docker only honors
# the .dockerignore at the build context root).
#
# STRICT ALLOWLIST style.
#
# Why: Railway's "Metal" builder uses incremental snapshot uploads. With a
# denylist .dockerignore, the snapshot diff algorithm was silently dropping
# paths that hadn't been touched in many commits (scraper/fixtures,
# scraper/scripts), causing COPY layers to fail with "/scraper/<dir>: not
# found" even though the files were on origin/main. An allowlist forces the
# snapshot manifest to include every explicitly-allowed path on every build,
# making the snapshot deterministic across rebuilds.

# Deny everything by default
*

# Root workspace metadata (needed for `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and
# for scraper/tsconfig.json's `extends: "../tsconfig.json"` reference).
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.json

# Scraper service — full source + fixtures (this is what ships)
!scraper

# Re-deny noise inside scraper
scraper/.env
scraper/.env.*
!scraper/.env.example
scraper/node_modules
scraper/dist
scraper/coverage
scraper/tests
scraper/eval
scraper/docs
scraper/scripts

# Packages — pnpm workspace needs every workspace package.json present to
# resolve the lockfile, even for packages we don't COPY into the image.
!packages
packages/*/src
packages/*/tests
packages/*/dist
packages/*/node_modules
packages/*/tsup.config.ts
packages/*/tsconfig.json
packages/*/CHANGELOG.md
packages/*/README.md

# Landing — only its package.json (same workspace-resolution reason as
# packages above). Docker requires un-excluding the parent directory before
# a file-level `!path/file` rule can reach in: allow landing/, deny all its
# contents, then re-allow the one file.
!landing
landing/*
!landing/package.json

# Global denies — never bake into any image
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.vitest-cache
**/coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
